00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:12.120
- [Kelly] I, yeah, it, well, it worked.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:12.953
It's happening.

00:00:12.953 --> 00:00:13.920
- Well, that's what I'm
celebrating in the holidays,

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:14.854
is Prince.

00:00:14.854 --> 00:00:16.020
- I know. I feel like every time I see you

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.573
it's the... we're celebrating holidays.

00:00:17.573 --> 00:00:19.028
- [Amy] We are!
- So many holidays.

00:00:19.028 --> 00:00:20.181
I'm always in a red dress when I'm...

00:00:20.181 --> 00:00:21.014
- [Amy] Yeah.

00:00:21.014 --> 00:00:21.847
- I swear I have other colors.

00:00:21.847 --> 00:00:23.640
- I'm always just covered
in some kind of like,

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.380
Christmas bow, like...

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.610
- [Kelly] This is like our tradition.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:27.443
- Yeah.

00:00:27.443 --> 00:00:28.380
- Alright. So last time we were here,

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.659
you said that you were going
to dance across the country.

00:00:30.659 --> 00:00:31.492
- I did?

00:00:31.492 --> 00:00:32.438
- For your 50th birthday.

00:00:32.438 --> 00:00:33.461
- Oh wow, I said that?

00:00:33.461 --> 00:00:34.360
- How was your dance?

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.640
- I said that?

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.900
- [Kelly] How was the dance?

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.386
- I had a big dance
party. I love to dance.

00:00:39.386 --> 00:00:40.546
We talked about this.

00:00:40.546 --> 00:00:41.379
- I know this about you, yes.

00:00:41.379 --> 00:00:42.750
- And I, I don't know if I said this then

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:46.260
but I find dancing at events and functions

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.870
a really good way to get rid of anxiety.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.095
- Yes. Because it's awkward. Yeah.

00:00:51.095 --> 00:00:52.800
- [Amy] Because it's
hard sometimes to talk.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:53.633
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:53.633 --> 00:00:56.583
- To people, even though that's your job.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.099
One of your 10 jobs.

00:00:59.099 --> 00:01:01.170
But, and sometimes it's like you wanna

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:02.100
just kind of move your body.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:06.120
So I find that more... dancing relaxes me.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:06.953
- Me too.

00:01:06.953 --> 00:01:07.786
- And when you're at a party, you're like

00:01:07.786 --> 00:01:09.750
"I can't talk right now. I have to dance."

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:10.583
Like, you know you have to...

00:01:10.583 --> 00:01:11.460
- [Kelly] Yes!
- Yeah.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.380
So I had a big dance
party for my birthday.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.213
- I love that.
- [Amy] Yeah.

00:01:14.213 --> 00:01:17.730
And I, yeah, I, I'm not
like a dancer per se,

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:19.050
but I love...
- [Amy] It doesn't matter.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.310
- [Kelly] I love moving my body.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.451
- Me too, me too.

00:01:21.451 --> 00:01:22.290
- I feel it feels so good.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:25.920
- I love shouting lyrics at my friends.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.530
- Yeah. Do you ever, usually when I'm...

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.370
usually when I'm doing this,
I get all the lyrics wrong.

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:32.520
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.050
It's like, oh, I didn't know those.

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:35.970
- That's part of the fun.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:37.260
- Not even, don't even have to be drunk.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.600
Just still don't get
them completely sober.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.130
- Yep, yep. And if you
don't, and if you...

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.960
if you mix it up, you give like a wink.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.460
So you're like, "I knew what it was".

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:45.293
- You're like, "I messed that up.

00:01:45.293 --> 00:01:46.260
I was just being funny."

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.280
- [Amy] Yeah. I'm just doing a remix.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.230
- I heard this about you,
which I think is funny

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:50.520
'cause it seems late in the game

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:51.960
to learn how to pluck your eyebrows,

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.343
But Tina Fey taught you?

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.140
Like, when did she...

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.580
did she teach you how
to pluck your eyebrows?

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:57.900
I'm like, how long have
you known each other?

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.160
- What if I was like, "44"?

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.380
- I was like, I was like...
it seemed late in the game.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.288
Like, when did y'all meet and this happen?

00:02:03.288 --> 00:02:04.380
- We were probably at that point,

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:08.670
we were probably touring
at, touring for Second City.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:10.470
So I was in my twenties for sure.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:11.303
- Oh, okay. Okay.

00:02:11.303 --> 00:02:12.136
- Yeah. I was in my twenties.

00:02:12.136 --> 00:02:13.170
- For some reason in my brain,

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.700
I just see y'all meeting at 30.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.830
And you were like, "so
how do you do this?"

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.140
- No. You know, you know Tina and Maya,

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.490
who I do "Baking It" with and like,

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:24.681
we've all now known each other
for 25 years almost. So...

00:02:24.681 --> 00:02:25.514
- That's awesome.

00:02:25.514 --> 00:02:26.940
- Yeah. Rachel Dratch,
all those people I met,

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.460
but Tina and I met in Chicago
in the nineties, so yeah.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.293
It must have been...

00:02:30.293 --> 00:02:32.130
And the nineties was a
different time, you know?

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:34.740
- I feel like people used to
pluck all their eyebrows off

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:35.573
at one point.

00:02:35.573 --> 00:02:37.047
- That's true. Yes. That's true.

00:02:37.047 --> 00:02:37.880
- It was a very thin line.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.860
- I have very, I've been told not to brag

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.190
but I've been told I
have very Irish eyebrows,

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:46.940
which means they're hardy.
- [Kelly] Yeah. I have...

00:02:48.247 --> 00:02:49.110
- And they're kind of strong.

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:50.179
- I do too.

00:02:50.179 --> 00:02:51.012
- [Amy] Do you too?

00:02:51.012 --> 00:02:51.845
- Yeah, you have to pluck away.

00:02:51.845 --> 00:02:52.860
There's a carpet up here.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:53.910
- [Amy] That's not a bad thing.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.560
But yeah, in the nineties
it was kind of tough.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:56.559
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:56.559 --> 00:02:58.140
- Now everyone's like, you know,

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:00.498
four day work week and do your
eyebrows however you want.

00:03:00.498 --> 00:03:01.331
Amazing. Again.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:01.331 --> 00:03:03.030
I love it. We're starting
to turn European.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:03.863
- Amazing.

00:03:03.863 --> 00:03:05.490
with this whole... yeah,
I love, I love that vibe.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:06.900
Yeah. I feel like every
time I go to Europe,

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:07.800
they're always on vacation.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.450
I'm like, "why did I not grow up here?"

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.283
- [Amy] Yeah.

00:03:10.283 --> 00:03:12.180
- I'm like, what? How are
you still on vacation?

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.190
- You should do Kelly Clarkson in Europe.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.900
And then the entire
week should be no shows.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.310
- Yeah. We just sit around

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.625
- We just have wine and...

00:03:18.625 --> 00:03:19.983
- Will you come to that show
and just hang out with wine?

00:03:19.983 --> 00:03:21.840
- Yes. And we walk around and we film it

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:22.957
just one hour a day and you're like,

00:03:22.957 --> 00:03:24.728
"This is it." And we're in Europe.

00:03:24.728 --> 00:03:25.561
- "And we're done".

00:03:25.561 --> 00:03:27.716
And now see us, we're gonna go take a nap.

00:03:27.716 --> 00:03:30.690
You teamed up, you said, with
Maya Rudolph for "Baking It."

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:32.550
- [Amy] Yes. Yes, the great Maya.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:33.660
- [Kelly] For people that don't know,

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.970
like what's the premise of
the show other than baking?

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.400
- Well, I filled in for the
great Andy Sandberg this year

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.040
who was, who did this season last year.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.640
But it's a baking show that's,
it's just goofball city.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:45.840
It's super fun.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.660
There's a lot of, we do a lot
of singing with each other

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.193
around other people.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:52.890
You know, because I think
I talked to you about this.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:54.930
I mean, you know, you're the
best singer in the world.

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:55.866
- I'm not, but thank you.

00:03:55.866 --> 00:03:57.090
- [Amy] Yes you are.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:01.320
And don't argue with me. But, um...

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.153
- Rude.

00:04:02.153 --> 00:04:02.986
- We love singing... rude.

00:04:02.986 --> 00:04:05.940
We love singing because, I
love singing because I'm like,

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:07.020
who cares, you know?

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:08.160
- I'm, that's me too.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.920
- I know, but we talked
about this because you...

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.270
when you're like, when
you do your soundcheck

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.860
you're like, "this matters".

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:15.963
You, you're a professional.

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:18.300
Let me make it clear.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.890
When you're not a professional singer,

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:21.570
you're like, "I don't
know, give it a try."

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:22.403
- Yeah.

00:04:22.403 --> 00:04:23.580
- So we goof around a lot.
- Yes.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.876
- And sing a lot and do
a lot of goofball stuff.

00:04:25.876 --> 00:04:26.930
- That's great. That's, yeah.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:29.340
- And then, oh, there's
also a baking competition.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:30.630
The added experience.
- [Kelly] There's a show.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:31.530
- There's a show, yeah.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:32.363
- No, but I love...

00:04:32.363 --> 00:04:34.500
so explain the judge...
there's the judges, right?

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:35.889
- Yeah. There's grannys.
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:04:35.889 --> 00:04:37.470
- We have grannys who
are the judging panels.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:38.303
- [Kelly] I love this.

00:04:38.303 --> 00:04:40.650
- And they're opinionated
and experienced grannys.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:43.740
They between them have tons
of years and experience

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:45.180
of cooking and baking and...
- Yeah.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.730
- They're teachers and you know, bloggers

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:48.563
and all this stuff.

00:04:48.563 --> 00:04:50.490
But they are, at the end of
the day, they're grandmas.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.050
And so they give it to you straight.

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:52.883
- Yes.

00:04:52.883 --> 00:04:54.090
- But they, it's a soft landing.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.410
They give it to you with a lot of love.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:56.580
- [Kelly] Okay.
- Yeah.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:58.260
And they, they're our judges

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:00.150
and they decide who stays and who goes.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.010
- I love that judging panel.
- [Amy] I know.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:02.850
- It's amazing.
- [Amy] Me too.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.020
It, it's so fun.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:06.720
It's so fun to hang out with
Maya. It's so fun to do.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.280
- [Kelly] That's so cool,
those solid relationships.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.750
You'd mentioned that you and Tina and Maya

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:10.650
have known each other for so long.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:13.020
Having those kind of solid
female relationships for so long.

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:14.012
- [Amy] For sure.

00:05:14.012 --> 00:05:14.845
- Kelly] That's incredible.

00:05:14.845 --> 00:05:15.678
- [Amy] So many.

00:05:15.678 --> 00:05:16.511
- [Kelly] Not everybody has that. Yeah.

00:05:16.511 --> 00:05:19.080
- [Amy] So many different
kinds of eyebrows we've had.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.670
- [Kelly] Together!
- [Amy] Together.

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:21.600
- Molding and shaping them together.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:24.000
- So many. At times just
one. At times just one.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.140
That we all share.

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:26.640
- But just the one uni.

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:28.830
So wait, so you and
Maya have a little song

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:29.663
in the opening credits.

00:05:29.663 --> 00:05:30.496
You're speaking about liking to sing.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.310
So I will show a little tape of this. Yes.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.810
- Oh, dear. Well, remember
I'm not a professional.

