00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:05.689
(explosion sound effect)

00:06:05.689 --> 00:06:09.791
(crowd cheering and applauding)

00:06:09.791 --> 00:06:14.040
- [Kelly] So the real question exactly,

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.250
the real question here
is what took longer,

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.871
learning and writing the
song, or the choreography?

00:06:19.871 --> 00:06:21.720
- Oh it's such a good question,

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:23.160
because the choreography we kept...

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:25.530
we kept going, let's
pull it back, like the...

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.401
Every time they would do
the the steps we'd be like,

00:06:27.401 --> 00:06:29.580
"is there a way where it
could just go like this?"

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.560
Like we just kept making
it slower and easier.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:32.970
- Easier to remember.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:34.920
- Yeah. So that was the
easiest choreography

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:36.600
we could get them to allow us to do.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:38.310
- My kind of choreography.
- Me too.

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:39.780
And from SNL you're so used to

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:42.259
just learning choreography
fast, but yet we were still like

00:06:42.259 --> 00:06:43.092
(dramatic heavy breathing)

00:06:43.092 --> 00:06:43.925
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:43.925 --> 00:06:45.180
- From the smallest choreography.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:47.280
- I know. And you're reminded...
that, that happens to me.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.180
When I haven't done a show for a while

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:50.400
and I'm reminded, I'm like, "oh, not 25."

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.660
- [Amy] Oh a hundred percent.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:53.610
- [Kelly] So wait, what's
been your biggest like,

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:54.870
disaster in the kitchen?

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:55.703
Which by the way,

00:06:55.703 --> 00:06:57.090
I don't know whose idea
the exploding cake was.

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:58.350
'Cause y'all have the ideas, right?

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.880
- Yeah, well we were joking that like

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:01.560
because we had two moms
on the show this year,

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:03.240
We were like, "we're
gonna blow some stuff up".

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.586
Like that was our joke. Like baking bad.

00:07:05.586 --> 00:07:06.885
- Yeah. Which I love.

00:07:06.885 --> 00:07:08.460
- So yeah, so we blew up some stuff.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:09.690
I have no idea how they did it.

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:10.830
They put something in it

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.170
and then just told us to stand back.

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:15.090
- Love.
- Yeah, which is...

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:18.510
But a disaster in the
kitchen? I don't know.

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:21.720
You know, I I, I think that
cooking and baking is like

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:23.340
low risk, high reward.

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:26.040
If it works, you feel
like a million bucks.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:26.873
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:07:26.873 --> 00:07:27.706
- And if it doesn't work,

00:07:27.706 --> 00:07:29.100
unless it's Thanksgiving, who cares?

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:29.933
- No, this is true.

00:07:29.933 --> 00:07:31.410
One time I, I think I've
said this on the show

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:32.820
but one time I made myself a cake

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:33.737
and I just wanted to kinda
be alone on my birthday.

00:07:33.737 --> 00:07:35.075
'Cause I was just always around people.

00:07:35.075 --> 00:07:35.908
- Yes.

00:07:35.908 --> 00:07:36.741
- [Kelly] And I was like, for my birthday,

00:07:36.741 --> 00:07:37.740
I just wanna be at my house alone.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:38.573
- Yes.

00:07:38.573 --> 00:07:41.490
I made myself a bread
cake because I looked over

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:43.680
and I was like, "there's the sugar".

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:45.120
And I had forgotten to put it in.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.800
But if you put icing on it...

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:47.633
- [Amy] It tastes fine.

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:48.466
- Totally fine.

00:07:48.466 --> 00:07:49.299
- It tastes fine.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:49.299 --> 00:07:51.810
I put the icing on it and I
was like, "bread cake is good".

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:55.380
Anyways, so, that's my
big fail. On my birthday.

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:57.180
- It seems like a success
because you were alone.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:58.972
- It was covered in icing and I was alone.

00:07:58.972 --> 00:07:59.805
- [Amy] Yeah. You were alone.

00:07:59.805 --> 00:08:02.160
- And watching Family
Feud, living my best dream.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.320
Yeah. It was just easy.
- [Amy] Yeah.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:05.610
- So wait, you have, I wanted to,

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:07.110
I want to bring this
up because a while ago

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:08.790
you gave a commencement speech at Harvard,

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:09.900
which is incredibly cool.
(audience applauding)

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:11.400
And you said something,
it was really cool.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:12.731
- Oh my God, yeah.

00:08:12.731 --> 00:08:13.564
- So you said

00:08:13.564 --> 00:08:15.660
"as you navigate through
the rest of your life,

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.370
be open to collaborations.

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:20.130
Other people's ideas are
often better than your own.

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:22.770
Find a group of people who
challenge and inspire you.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.800
Spend a lot of time with them
and it will change your life."

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:27.950
I think this is the best advice.

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:29.490
(audience applauding)
- It's true.

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:30.840
- [Kelly] It is! I... people always,

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:31.807
I don't know if they look and you and go,

00:08:31.807 --> 00:08:32.967
"oh my God, your career,
you've done so well".

00:08:32.967 --> 00:08:33.800
And I'm like, yeah.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:36.480
A team of people like, like
there's a whole group of us

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:37.740
that have made all of this happen.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:38.573
- [Amy] Yeah.

00:08:38.573 --> 00:08:39.530
- Like it's so smart to tell people to do.

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:40.650
- I, I think there's...

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:42.690
I think you can do
anything with a good team.

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:43.523
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:43.523 --> 00:08:44.356
- You can do anything.

00:08:44.356 --> 00:08:46.320
And a good team is a
team that everyone feels

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:48.630
like they're... they know
what they're working for.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:49.463
- Yeah.

00:08:49.463 --> 00:08:51.390
- [Amy] And also they don't,

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:53.460
there's not a lot of
like, "that's not my job".

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:55.830
A good team is a team that works together.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:58.214
I've been really lucky in my
life to be on many of them.

00:08:58.214 --> 00:08:59.047
- Me too.

00:08:59.047 --> 00:09:01.170
- Yeah. And I feel like because of that

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:02.730
I've been able to do all
these different things.

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:04.560
If you have a team of people and it's...

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.570
could be your family, your
partner, the people you work with

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.370
you have people who know you, support you.

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:09.203
- Yeah.

00:09:09.203 --> 00:09:10.685
- [Amy] Care about you...
You can do anything.

00:09:10.685 --> 00:09:12.090
And there's no better feeling than like,

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:13.650
failing and successing,

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:15.450
like success and failure with someone.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:16.283
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:16.283 --> 00:09:19.080
- It's so, it feels so
good to win as a team.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:20.250
- Yeah.

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.260
- And it's a lot less lonely when you...

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:23.490
- [Kelly] When you fail.
- When you fail. Yeah.

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:24.660
- [Kelly] And we all do, that's the thing.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.520
I think that people frown
upon it but it's like,

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:27.900
well that's the time I
think you learn the most.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:30.347
Not when you win. So yeah.
I think that's alright.

00:09:30.347 --> 00:09:32.430
- And I think that
working well with others

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:35.940
is a, a really valuable skill.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:37.560
- That I think is really important.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:38.943
I know it's important with
the people I work with.

00:09:38.943 --> 00:09:40.740
That you like to work with other people.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:42.450
- That's why your shows,
a lot of that is like

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:43.500
your shows that I love watching,

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:44.430
It's always like teams of people

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:45.780
like working together to make
something happen at the end

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:47.370
and there's a product and it's fun.

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:49.440
- Yeah. I think that's why
workplace comedies are fun

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:50.880
is 'cause it's a team of people

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:52.710
that would never choose to be together.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:53.543
- Yeah.

00:09:54.386 --> 00:09:56.520
- And you're like, wow,
we have nothing in common.

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:57.353
Let's make this happen.

00:09:57.353 --> 00:09:58.743
- And yet we're succeeding!

